WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:09.095
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.395 --> 00:00:14.949
Unit sixteen: Goal Setting. Today you will talk about future achievements with the future perfect.

4
00:00:15.249 --> 00:00:17.890
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:22.182
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:24.134
SMART goal.

7
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:30.714
SMART goal means a goal that is specific, measurable, achievable, relevant and time-bound.

8
00:00:31.317 --> 00:00:33.781
Pass B1 by June is a SMART goal.

9
00:00:34.383 --> 00:00:37.163
Your turn. Say: SMART goal.

10
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.198
SMART goal.

11
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.009
Milestone.

12
00:00:44.017 --> 00:00:47.096
Milestone means an important step toward a goal.

13
00:00:47.683 --> 00:00:49.718
Finishing Book 2 was a milestone.

14
00:00:50.317 --> 00:00:53.073
Your turn. Say: Milestone.

15
00:00:55.933 --> 00:00:57.027
Milestone.

16
00:00:57.783 --> 00:00:59.017
Action plan.

17
00:01:00.017 --> 00:01:03.038
Action plan means a list of steps to reach a goal.

18
00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.812
My action plan has five steps.

19
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:09.092
Your turn. Say: Action plan.

20
00:01:11.933 --> 00:01:13.201
Action plan.

21
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.323
Accountability.

22
00:01:16.317 --> 00:01:20.034
Accountability means being responsible for your actions and results.

23
00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:23.253
A study partner gives me accountability.

24
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.839
Your turn. Say: Accountability.

25
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.084
Accountability.

26
00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:32.898
Motivation.

27
00:01:33.883 --> 00:01:36.997
Motivation means the reason or energy to do something.

28
00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:39.699
My family is my motivation.

29
00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:42.982
Your turn. Say: Motivation.

30
00:01:45.833 --> 00:01:46.997
Motivation.

31
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.041
Progress tracker.

32
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.536
Progress tracker means a chart that shows your progress.

33
00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.660
I tick my progress tracker every day.

34
00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.494
Your turn. Say: Progress tracker.

35
00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:04.590
Progress tracker.

36
00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:06.339
Obstacle.

37
00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.953
Obstacle means something that blocks your way.

38
00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.608
Laziness is my biggest obstacle.

39
00:02:13.217 --> 00:02:15.765
Your turn. Say: Obstacle.

40
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:19.740
Obstacle.

41
00:02:20.483 --> 00:02:21.508
Achievement.

42
00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:25.375
Achievement means something good you did with effort.

43
00:02:25.983 --> 00:02:28.145
Getting a scholarship was an achievement.

44
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.693
Your turn. Say: Achievement.

45
00:02:34.533 --> 00:02:35.476
Achievement.

46
00:02:36.217 --> 00:02:37.705
Long-term vision.

47
00:02:38.717 --> 00:02:41.773
Long-term vision means what you want your future to look like.

48
00:02:42.383 --> 00:02:44.859
My long-term vision is to be a doctor.

49
00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.381
Your turn. Say: Long-term vision.

50
00:02:51.233 --> 00:02:52.606
Long-term vision.

51
00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:54.583
Short-term goal.

52
00:02:55.583 --> 00:02:58.372
Short-term goal means a goal for the near future.

53
00:02:58.983 --> 00:03:01.819
My short-term goal is to read one book a month.

54
00:03:02.417 --> 00:03:05.580
Your turn. Say: Short-term goal.

55
00:03:08.433 --> 00:03:10.027
Short-term goal.

56
00:03:10.783 --> 00:03:11.610
Commitment.

57
00:03:12.617 --> 00:03:15.382
Commitment means a promise to work hard on something.

58
00:03:15.983 --> 00:03:18.041
Learning English needs commitment.

59
00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.326
Your turn. Say: Commitment.

60
00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:25.121
Commitment.

61
00:03:25.883 --> 00:03:26.792
Growth.

62
00:03:27.783 --> 00:03:29.922
Growth means becoming better over time.

63
00:03:30.517 --> 00:03:32.272
I can see my growth this year.

64
00:03:32.883 --> 00:03:35.187
Your turn. Say: Growth.

65
00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:38.663
Growth.

66
00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:43.048
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:43.883 --> 00:03:46.463
Visal, what is your SMART goal this year?

68
00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:50.130
To pass the B1 exam by June.

69
00:03:51.217 --> 00:03:52.972
What's your action plan?

70
00:03:54.083 --> 00:03:58.057
I study one hour a day, and I use a progress tracker.

71
00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.417
And what will you have done by next year?

72
00:04:02.517 --> 00:04:06.339
By next year, I will have achieved this goal and started B2!

73
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.047
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:09.883 --> 00:04:12.278
Grammar focus: Future perfect.

75
00:04:12.578 --> 00:04:13.753
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:17.204
By next year, I will have achieved this goal.

77
00:04:18.117 --> 00:04:20.348
By June, she will have finished the book.

78
00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.946
By 2030, we will have graduated.

79
00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:29.245
Use the future perfect for actions that will be finished before a time in the future.

80
00:04:29.983 --> 00:04:34.319
Be careful! Don't say: By next year, I will achieved this goal.

81
00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:39.729
Say: By next year, I will have achieved this goal.

82
00:04:40.029 --> 00:04:43.248
The future perfect is 'will have' + past participle.

83
00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.767
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:48.846
My SMART Goal.

85
00:04:49.146 --> 00:04:52.690
Setting a SMART goal with clear milestones keeps me accountable.

86
00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:57.557
My action plan has short-term goals and a long-term vision.

87
00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:01.100
Tracking progress keeps my motivation high.

88
00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.866
When I face an obstacle, I remember my commitment.

89
00:05:05.867 --> 00:05:09.770
By next year, I will have achieved my goal, and I will see real growth.

90
00:05:10.867 --> 00:05:15.135
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:15.983 --> 00:05:18.145
By June, I will have blank the course.

92
00:05:18.445 --> 00:05:22.238
A, finished. B, finish. C, finishing.

93
00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.509
The answer is A: finished.

94
00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:31.184
An important step toward a goal is a blank.

95
00:05:31.484 --> 00:05:35.509
A, milestone. B, obstacle. C, motivation.

96
00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:41.020
The answer is A: milestone.

97
00:05:42.183 --> 00:05:44.345
Something that blocks your way is an blank.

98
00:05:44.645 --> 00:05:48.264
A, obstacle. B, achievement. C, action plan.

99
00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.962
The answer is A: obstacle.

100
00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:58.341
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:59.183 --> 00:06:01.752
What is one SMART goal you have set for yourself?

102
00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:12.074
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:12.374 --> 00:06:21.551
My SMART goal is to read twelve English books this year, one each month. By December, I will have read all twelve.

104
00:06:21.851 --> 00:06:23.583
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:24.483 --> 00:06:28.645
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and future perfect.

106
00:06:28.945 --> 00:06:33.060
Today's value is ambition. Dream big and work hard for your future.

107
00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:36.105
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:36.405 --> 00:06:39.081
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

